    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0466" n="456" xml:id="pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.1/9601a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-02T13:00:00-04:00">December 2, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1731. From the Secretary of the Treasury for Adler.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Ambassador Wei has informed the Treasury that prices in China are no
                        longer rising but, because of gold sales, have in fact begun to
                        decline.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Telegraph reply of your views and comments on this matter is requested by
                        Treasury. [Morgenthau.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
